# Copy this file to .env (in this blockchain/ folder) before deploying to a
# real network. .env is gitignored - never commit real values.
#
# Only needed for `npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.js --network sepolia`.
# Deploying to --network localhost (a Hardhat node on your own machine)
# needs neither of these - see the README's local-dev instructions.

# --- Sepolia RPC endpoint ---
# A JSON-RPC URL for the Sepolia testnet. Quickest, zero-signup option:
#   SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com
# More reliable for repeated use (free tier, requires a signup):
#   SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://eth-sepolia.g.alchemy.com/v2/<your-alchemy-key>
#   SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://sepolia.infura.io/v3/<your-infura-key>
SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=

# --- Deployer wallet ---
# The private key of a TESTNET-ONLY wallet funded with a small amount of
# Sepolia ETH (free from a faucet, e.g. https://www.alchemy.com/faucets/ethereum-sepolia
# or https://faucet.quicknode.com/ethereum/sepolia - most require the wallet
# to hold a small amount of real mainnet ETH first, to deter abuse).
# Whichever wallet deploys the contract becomes AuditLedger.sol's
# `authorizedServer` (see the onlyServer modifier) - the backend's
# DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY (backend/.env) must be this SAME key, or every
# on-chain write will revert with "Unauthorized".
#
# NEVER use a wallet that holds real funds or reuse this key anywhere else.
# Generate a fresh one just for this (e.g. `npx hardhat vars set` or any
# wallet tool's "create new account") rather than repurposing a personal one.
PRIVATE_KEY=
